body:
I've just tried with master code and it's all fine. I've used basic app.

`basic/config/web.php`:

``` php
'mail' => [
    'class' => 'yii\swiftmailer\Mailer',
    // it doesn't matter if it will write to file or actually send email, right?
    'useFileTransport' => true,
],
'log' => [
    'traceLevel' => YII_DEBUG ? 3 : 0,
    'targets' => [
        [
            'class' => 'yii\log\FileTarget',
            'levels' => ['error', 'warning'],
        ],
        [
            'class' => 'yii\log\EmailTarget',
            'mail' =>'mail',
            'levels' => ['error', 'warning'],
            'message' => [
                'to' => ['adress1@gmail.com', 'address2@gmail.com'],
                'subject' => ' Frontend LOG',
            ],
        ],
    ],
],
```

`controller/SiteController.php`:

``` php
public function actionIndex()
{
    Yii::getLogger()->log('test', Logger::LEVEL_ERROR);
    return $this->render('index');
}
```
